From 2fa57eaf7a7d4ebd565ff34fa517d3991fe6ce3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gogo <gogo@bluedynamics.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:59:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] Fix blob collisions in budget mode

Colliding blobs were set to shape group 0 to mean "no group", but the
chipmunk Ruby wrapper stores rb_obj_id(value) as the group, which is
never 0. All colliding blobs ended up in one group, and shapes in the
same group never collide, so nothing collided at all.

- rb_cpShape: group = nil now means CP_NO_GROUP.
- Engine: colliding blobs get group nil; the collider limit starts at
  1000 instead of 0 before the first physics step.

Checked through Engine#add_blob/#set_collider with two blobs head-on:
colliding pairs bounce (also after being rotated out and back in),
pairs with a passive blob pass through. With real collisions, at 1500
blobs/s: everything colliding ~34 ms physics/frame; budget mode 5-7 ms
with 850-1500 colliding and 35-40% of blobs bouncing back.

Requires bin/setup to rebuild the vendored chipmunk.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013kYwHzrj5ef427USqzf3UF
